Z||000015||stsmithgt||09-11-2000||11:34 AM||||OK. I hate to say it, but I kinda nose how that guy feels.  What are the odds?  I even consider myself fairly inteligent, but my night vision could be better.  <BR>A buddy of mine years ago had a 70 mustang with an after market antenna that went along the windshield pillar. it was long enough to reach my nose when I tried getting into the car one night.  What an explosion of pain in the head and you don't even know why for a moment.  My eyeballs felt like they were goig to pop out. I thought it went into one of my eye sockets.  After the main shock of it all, it turned out my head is made of something tougher than a chrome ball on an antenna.  No blood.  No damage.  It kept me from sitting down too.  Just thinking about it makes my sinuses hurt.  I wouldn't wish that shock on anybody.  There's a lot of nerves that scream at you when that happens.  I suppose my buddy was lucky I didn't tear that antenna off his car, but my eyes were watering so much, I couldn't see well for awhile.  I had more than my share of alcohol that night to cover the pain.  Sometimes you can just have one of those days. ||||reg||8
